        'The earliest source naming the sisters is the Hou Hanshu of Fan Ye (398 - 445), in chapter 24 (biography of Ma Yuan) and chapter 86 (account of the Southern Man). The Shuijing zhu of Li Daoyuan (early 6th century) also quotes the lost Jiaozhou waiyu ji. On the Vietnamese side, Lê Văn Hưu (1272) and Ngô Sĩ Liên (1479) gave the sisters their own annal, the Annal of Queen Trưng in the Đại Việt sử ký toàn thư. No text written by a contemporary in Jiaozhi survives.',
